ne":3,"text":"Direct Remote mode detects browser-authenticated Hermes dashboards and connects without exposing OAuth credentials to renderer code."},{"markdown":"The public dashboard status endpoint and raw-gateway health endpoint select token or OAuth behavior automatically for direct Remote connections.","startLine":7,"endLine":7,"text":"The public dashboard status endpoint and raw-gateway health endpoint select token or OAuth behavior automatically for direct Remote connections."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#probeRemoteAuthMode]] reads `/api/status`; `auth_required: true` selects OAuth. A `404` or `405` then probes `/health` with the supplied `API_SERVER_KEY`: a healthy response or an explicit `401`/`403` identifies the raw token gateway. Other probe failures remain errors rather than transport guesses.","startLine":9,"endLine":9,"text":"src/main/remote-oauth.ts#probeRemoteAuthMode reads /api/status; auth_required: true selects OAuth. A 404 or 405 then probes /health with the supplied API_SERVER_KEY: a healthy response or an explicit 401/403 identifies the raw token gateway. Other probe failures remain errors rather than transport guesses."},{"markdown":"Configured reverse-proxy URL credentials become Basic headers for both discovery routes, with encoded userinfo decoded before transmission. Public status never receives the dashboard token; raw health retains Bearer authentication when no proxy credentials are configured.","startLine":11,"endLine":11,"text":"Configured reverse-proxy URL credentials become Basic headers for both discovery routes, with encoded userinfo decoded before transmission. Public status never receives the dashboard token; raw health retains Bearer authentication when no proxy credentials are configured."},{"markdown":"The first-run `connect-remote-gateway` operation in [[src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers]] owns detection, authentication, validation, and configuration commit as one main-process transaction. OAuth opens the dedicated login window before saving; token mode verifies `/health`; either failure leaves the previous connection configuration untouched. [[src/renderer/src/screens/Welcome/Welcome.tsx#Welcome]] surfaces that single operation and explains that the remote key comes from `API_SERVER_KEY` in the remote `~/.hermes/.env`.","startLine":13,"endLine":13,"text":"The first-run connect-remote-gateway operation in src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers owns detection, authentication, validation, and configuration commit as one main-process transaction. OAuth opens the dedicated login window before saving; token mode verifies /health; either failure leaves the previous connection configuration untouched. src/renderer/src/screens/Welcome/Welcome.tsx#Welcome surfaces that single operation and explains that the remote key comes from API_SERVER_KEY in the remote ~/.hermes/.env."},{"markdown":"The public startup probe uses `/api/status` without a stored token after OAuth is selected, avoiding the authenticated `/health` redirect and stale-token false negatives.","startLine":15,"endLine":15,"text":"The public startup probe uses /api/status without a stored token after OAuth is selected, avoiding the authenticated /health redirect and stale-token false negatives."},{"markdown":"Main-process Node HTTPS and onboarding fetch include trusted operating-system roots without weakening certificate or hostname verification.","startLine":19,"endLine":19,"text":"Main-process Node HTTPS and onboarding fetch include trusted operating-system roots without weakening certificate or hostname verification."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/system-ca-trust.ts#initializeSystemCertificateTrust]] unions `tls.getCACertificates(\"default\")` with `\"system\"` and installs the deduplicated result. Existing bundled, extra, and custom defaults remain trusted. The side-effect import is first in [[src/main/index.ts]], before consumers can cache TLS sessions. Electron cookie-backed OAuth transport is unchanged.","startLine":21,"endLine":21,"text":"src/main/system-ca-trust.ts#initializeSystemCertificateTrust unions tls.getCACertificates(\"default\") with \"system\" and installs the deduplicated result. Existing bundled, extra, and custom defaults remain trusted. The side-effect import is first in src/main/index.ts, before consumers can cache TLS sessions. Electron cookie-backed OAuth transport is unchanged."},{"markdown":"Both APIs are feature-detected. Older development Node runtimes retain their existing defaults; a system-store lookup or setter failure logs a warning and keeps verification enabled. The packaged Electron 44 runtime supports the APIs. Node documents the getter from 22.15 and the setter from 22.19 (also 24.5) in its [TLS API reference](https://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tlssetdefaultcacertificatescerts). Trust changes apply to the main thread; no OS trust store or user configuration is modified.","startLine":23,"endLine":23,"text":"Both APIs are feature-detected. Older development Node runtimes retain their existing defaults; a system-store lookup or setter failure logs a warning and keeps verification enabled. The packaged Electron 44 runtime supports the APIs. Node documents the getter from 22.15 and the setter from 22.19 (also 24.5) in its TLS API reference. Trust changes apply to the main thread; no OS trust store or user configuration is modified."},{"markdown":"A private/self-signed root must already be trusted by the operating system or supplied through supported Node extra-CA configuration. Arbitrary untrusted endpoints still fail. Native OS-store installation is outside the isolated regression proof.","startLine":25,"endLine":25,"text":"A private/self-signed root must already be trusted by the operating system or supplied through supported Node extra-CA configuration. Arbitrary untrusted endpoints still fail. Native OS-store installation is outside the isolated regression proof."},{"markdown":"OAuth cookies live only in a dedicated persistent Electron session owned by main process.","startLine":29,"endLine":29,"text":"OAuth cookies live only in a dedicated persistent Electron session owned by main process."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#REMOTE_OAUTH_PARTITION]] identifies `persist:hermes-remote-oauth`. [[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#openRemoteOAuthLogin]] opens sandboxed `/login`; preload exposes only login, logout, probe, and signed-in state.","startLine":31,"endLine":31,"text":"src/main/remote-oauth.ts#REMOTE_OAUTH_PARTITION identifies persist:hermes-remote-oauth. src/main/remote-oauth.ts#openRemoteOAuthLogin opens sandboxed /login; preload exposes only login, logout, probe, and signed-in state."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#requestRemoteOAuthJson]] uses Electron `net` with that session and `useSessionCookies: true`. Cookies, refresh tokens, and WebSocket tickets never enter renderer state or desktop configuration.","startLine":33,"endLine":33,"text":"src/main/remote-oauth.ts#requestRemoteOAuthJson uses Electron net with that session and useSessionCookies: true. Cookies, refresh tokens, and WebSocket tickets never enter renderer state or desktop configuration."},{"markdown":"After the browser flow returns, [[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#connectionConfigAfterRemoteOAuthLogin]] re-reads the current configuration. It commits OAuth mode only when Remote mode and the normalized gateway URL still match, preserving newer settings.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"After the browser flow returns, src/main/remote-oauth.ts#connectionConfigAfterRemoteOAuthLogin re-reads the current configuration. It commits OAuth mode only when Remote mode and the normalized gateway URL still match, preserving newer settings."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/hermes.ts#getRemoteAuthHeader]] suppresses stored Remote bearer keys whenever OAuth is selected. The key may remain saved for later token mode, but OAuth chat and auxiliary requests cannot reuse it.","startLine":37,"endLine":37,"text":"src/main/hermes.ts#getRemoteAuthHeader suppresses stored Remote bearer keys whenever OAuth is selected. The key may remain saved for later token mode, but OAuth chat and auxiliary requests cannot reuse it."},{"markdown":"Every OAuth WebSocket attempt receives a new single-use ticket immediately before connection.","startLine":41,"endLine":41,"text":"Every OAuth WebSocket attempt receives a new single-use ticket immediately before connection."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/dashboard.ts#freshDashboardWebSocketUrl]] calls [[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#mintRemoteOAuthWsTicket]] for OAuth connections. Readiness probing consumes its own ticket; renderer reconnects request another through bounded IPC.","startLine":43,"endLine":43,"text":"src/main/dashboard.ts#freshDashboardWebSocketUrl calls src/main/remote-oauth.ts#mintRemoteOAuthWsTicket for OAuth connections. Readiness probing consumes its own ticket; renderer reconnects request another through bounded IPC."},{"markdown":"For non-loopback HTTP gateways, [[src/main/dashboard-websocket-relay.ts#createLoopbackWebSocketRelay]] proxies one WebSocket through a random-capability loopback URL. The renderer CSP permits loopback WebSockets, never arbitrary `ws:` origins.","startLine":45,"endLine":45,"text":"For non-loopback HTTP gateways, src/main/dashboard-websocket-relay.ts#createLoopbackWebSocketRelay proxies one WebSocket through a random-capability loopback URL. The renderer CSP permits loopback WebSockets, never arbitrary ws: origins."},{"markdown":"Remote session history uses the same selected authentication transport as management APIs.","startLine":49,"endLine":49,"text":"Remote session history uses the same selected authentication transport as management APIs."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-sessions.ts#remoteRequestJson]] routes direct OAuth session lists, search, messages, media, titles, and deletion through the persistent cookie partition. Token and SSH session requests send `X-Hermes-Session-Token` plus `Authorization: Bearer` for gateway compatibility. When the configured URL contains Basic credentials for a reverse proxy, Node supplies Basic authorization and the dashboard still receives its separate session-token header. The gateway API key and dashboard session token remain distinct credentials; adding a header does not make them interchangeable.","startLine":51,"endLine":51,"text":"src/main/remote-sessions.ts#remoteRequestJson routes direct OAuth session lists, search, messages, media, titles, and deletion through the persistent cookie partition. Token and SSH session requests send X-Hermes-Session-Token plus Authorization: Bearer for gateway compatibility. When the configured URL contains Basic credentials for a reverse proxy, Node supplies Basic authorization and the dashboard still receives its separate session-token header. The gateway API key and dashboard session token remain distinct credentials; adding a header does not make them interchangeable."},{"markdown":"Direct Remote management features share one main-process request client that selects cookie or token authentication without exposing reusable credentials through IPC.","startLine":55,"endLine":55,"text":"Direct Remote management features share one main-process request client that selects cookie or token authentication without exposing reusable credentials through IPC."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-api.ts#remoteDashboardRequestJson]] resolves `auto` through the public status probe, routes OAuth through the persistent Electron partition, and routes token mode through the shared session request client with the same Bearer/Basic handling. Unexpected probe failures never guess another transport or fall back to local state.","startLine":57,"endLine":57,"text":"src/main/remote-api.ts#remoteDashboardRequestJson resolves auto through the public status probe, routes OAuth through the persistent Electron partition, and routes token mode through the shared session request client with the same Bearer/Basic handling. Unexpected probe failures never guess another transport or fall back to local state."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-api.ts#RemoteDashboardApiError]] normalizes HTTP status for feature adapters. A `404` marks only that feature unsupported; OAuth login-required errors retain their original reauthentication signal.","startLine":59,"endLine":59,"text":"src/main/remote-api.ts#RemoteDashboardApiError normalizes HTTP status for feature adapters. A 404 marks only that feature unsupported; OAuth login-required errors retain their original reauthentication signal."},{"markdown":"Missing or expired OAuth sessions stop Remote chat and request browser sign-in without falling back to local state or legacy `/v1`.","startLine":63,"endLine":63,"text":"Missing or expired OAuth sessions stop Remote chat and request browser sign-in without falling back to local state or legacy /v1."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport]] marks OAuth login-required errors as dashboard-reachable failures. Settings hides Legacy transport for OAuth and provides Sign in and Sign out actions.","startLine":65,"endLine":65,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport marks OAuth login-required errors as dashboard-reachable failures. Settings hides Legacy transport for OAuth and provides Sign in and Sign out actions."},{"markdown":"Remote Skills uses cookie-aware fetch, while MCP uses the authenticated management request boundary. Both retain the selected profile and keep credentials in the main process.","startLine":69,"endLine":69,"text":"Remote Skills uses cookie-aware fetch, while MCP uses the authenticated management request boundary. Both retain the selected profile and keep credentials in the main process."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-oauth.ts#remoteAuthFetch]] accepts the connection snapshot used to build the Skills URL and headers, preventing an intervening selection change from choosing another target's authentication. Explicit token connections retain the caller's headers.","startLine":71,"endLine":71,"text":"src/main/remote-oauth.ts#remoteAuthFetch accepts the connection snapshot used to build the Skills URL and headers, preventing an intervening selection change from choosing another target's authentication. Explicit token connections retain the caller's headers."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx#Layout]] mounts Skills separately for each connection and profile, discarding the previous target's list and selection before install or uninstall controls become usable.","startLine":73,"endLine":73,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx#Layout mounts Skills separately for each connection and profile, discarding the previous target's list and selection before install or uninstall controls become usable."},{"markdown":"Explicit token dashboards without a key retain anonymous, profile-scoped MCP access, as does auto mode after the management boundary identifies a keyless token dashboard. OAuth failures never fall back to anonymous requests.","startLine":75,"endLine":75,"text":"Explicit token dashboards without a key retain anonymous, profile-scoped MCP access, as does auto mode after the management boundary identifies a keyless token dashboard. OAuth failures never fall back to anonymous requests."},{"markdown":"Focused tests protect credential isolation, automatic routing, ticket freshness, no-fallback behavior, and Settings presentation.","startLine":79,"endLine":79,"text":"Focused tests protect credential isolation, automatic routing, ticket freshness, no-fallback behavior, and Settings presentation."},{"markdown":"Session recognition accepts Hermes access or refresh cookie names in every deploy shape — bare, `__Host-` (direct HTTPS), `__Secure-` (path prefix), or `<tenant>_`-prefixed — and keeps cookie-backed requests inside the selected Electron partition.","startLine":83,"endLine":83,"text":"Session recognition accepts Hermes access or refresh cookie names in every deploy shape — bare, __Host- (direct HTTPS), __Secure- (path prefix), or <tenant>_-prefixed — and keeps cookie-backed requests inside the selected Electron partition."},{"markdown":"Session requests succeed against HTTP servers that accept only Bearer authentication or only the dedicated session header, preserving compatibility across gateway versions.","startLine":87,"endLine":87,"text":"Session requests succeed against HTTP servers that accept only Bearer authentication or only the dedicated session header, preserving compatibility across gateway versions."},{"markdown":"URLs containing proxy credentials retain Basic authorization while the dashboard receives its session token separately, preventing the compatibility header from breaking existing authenticated proxies.","startLine":91,"endLine":91,"text":"URLs containing proxy credentials retain Basic authorization while the dashboard receives its session token separately, preventing the compatibility header from breaking existing authenticated proxies."},{"markdown":"OAuth status requires a signed-in cookie session, authenticates REST without token headers, and probes WebSocket with a disposable ticket.","startLine":95,"endLine":95,"text":"OAuth status requires a signed-in cookie session, authenticates REST without token headers, and probes WebSocket with a disposable ticket."},{"markdown":"When `/api/status` is absent, a reachable or key-protected `/health` endpoint identifies token mode, while unrelated health failures remain user-visible connection errors.","startLine":99,"endLine":99,"text":"When /api/status is absent, a reachable or key-protected /health endpoint identifies token mode, while unrelated health failures remain user-visible connection errors."},{"markdown":"First-run Remote setup persists OAuth only after browser sign-in and token mode only after health validation; cancellation or failure preserves the prior connection configuration.","startLine":103,"endLine":103,"text":"First-run Remote setup persists OAuth only after browser sign-in and token mode only after health validation; cancellation or failure preserves the prior connection configuration."},{"markdown":"Every initial or reconnect attempt requests a new ticket URL, while token dashboards retain their stable token URL.","startLine":107,"endLine":107,"text":"Every initial or reconnect attempt requests a new ticket URL, while token dashboards retain their stable token URL."},{"markdown":"Login-required Remote chat errors reach user-visible failure handling and never enter legacy `/v1` fallback.","startLine":111,"endLine":111,"text":"Login-required Remote chat errors reach user-visible failure handling and never enter legacy /v1 fallback."},{"markdown":"Settings probes auth automatically, shows browser sign-in for OAuth, preserves token input for token gateways, and handles cancellation without false connected state.","startLine":115,"endLine":115,"text":"Settings probes auth automatically, shows browser sign-in for OAuth, preserves token input for token gateways, and handles cancellation without false connected state."},{"markdown":"OAuth login preserves settings changed while the browser is open and rejects completion when the selected gateway or connection mode changed.","startLine":119,"endLine":119,"text":"OAuth login preserves settings changed while the browser is open and rejects completion when the selected gateway or connection mode changed."},{"markdown":"Insecure remote WebSockets use a one-shot loopback relay with an unguessable path, while renderer CSP excludes the wildcard `ws:` source.","startLine":123,"endLine":123,"text":"Insecure remote WebSockets use a one-shot loopback relay with an unguessable path, while renderer CSP excludes the wildcard ws: source."},{"markdown":"Once a Remote connection resolves to OAuth, shared request headers omit any stored token while token and SSH authentication remain unchanged.","startLine":127,"endLine":127,"text":"Once a Remote connection resolves to OAuth, shared request headers omit any stored token while token and SSH authentication remain unchanged."},{"markdown":"Management requests resolve `auto` before selecting token or OAuth transport, preserve profile scoping, skip probing for explicit modes, reject non-Remote callers, and retain OAuth login-required errors for reauthentication.","startLine":131,"endLine":131,"text":"Management requests resolve auto before selecting token or OAuth transport, preserve profile scoping, skip probing for explicit modes, reject non-Remote callers, and retain OAuth login-required errors for reauthentication."},{"markdown":"Token and OAuth HTTP failures expose the same structured status, with `404` identified as an unsupported feature instead of an application-wide connection failure.","startLine":135,"endLine":135,"text":"Token and OAuth HTTP failures expose the same structured status, with 404 identified as an unsupported feature instead of an application-wide connection failure."},{"markdown":"Cookie-aware auxiliary requests use the caller's captured connection even after the active selection changes, keeping request authentication aligned with the original URL and profile.","startLine":139,"endLine":139,"text":"Cookie-aware auxiliary requests use the caller's captured connection even after the active selection changes, keeping request authentication aligned with the original URL and profile."},{"markdown":"Explicit token dashboards without configured keys can list MCP servers anonymously for a named profile, preserving open-gateway compatibility without weakening OAuth authentication.","startLine":143,"endLine":143,"text":"Explicit token dashboards without configured keys can list MCP servers anonymously for a named profile, preserving open-gateway compatibility without weakening OAuth authentication."},{"markdown":"Automatic detection forwards configured Basic proxy credentials to status and raw-health probes without putting userinfo in fetch URLs, while non-proxy raw gateways retain their Bearer header.","startLine":147,"endLine":147,"text":"Automatic detection forwards configured Basic proxy credentials to status and raw-health probes without putting userinfo in fetch URLs, while non-proxy raw gateways retain their Bearer header."},{"markdown":"Extending system trust retains bundled, extra, and existing custom roots, deduplicates overlaps, and leaves the original selection unchanged.","startLine":151,"endLine":151,"text":"Extending system trust retains bundled, extra, and existing custom roots, deduplicates overlaps, and leaves the original selection unchanged."},{"markdown":"A runtime missing either CA getter or setter keeps its existing trust rather than partially changing certificate validation.","startLine":155,"endLine":155,"text":"A runtime missing either CA getter or setter keeps its existing trust rather than partially changing certificate validation."},{"markdown":"A failed system-store read never invokes the setter or enables a permissive certificate or hostname fallback.","startLine":159,"endLine":159,"text":"A failed system-store read never invokes the setter or enables a permissive certificate or hostname fallback."},{"markdown":"A setter rejection is reported as unavailable without changing any request verification options.","startLine":163,"endLine":163,"text":"A setter rejection is reported as unavailable without changing any request verification options."},{"markdown":"An actual Electron run-as-Node child loads the real main entry before networking consumers, trusts a temporary system root for shared HTTPS and onboarding fetch, preserves extra CAs, and rejects unrelated roots and hostname mismatches.","startLine":167,"endLine":167,"text":"An actual Electron run-as-Node child loads the real main entry before networking consumers, trusts a temporary system root for shared HTTPS and onboarding fetch, preserves extra CAs, and rejects unrelated roots and hostname mismatches."},{"markdown":"